<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anguilla</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anguilla is a low coral island in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leeward-islands">Leeward Islands</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-overseas-territories">British Overseas Territory</a>. English settlers arrived from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Kitts</a> in 1650, and in 1882 it was joined with Saint Kitts and Nevis in a single colony. Resenting rule from Saint Kitts, Anguillans rebelled in 1967 and declared independence; after British intervention in 1969 it became a separate dependency again, formally from 1980.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anguilla.jpg" alt="Anguilla" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This work created by the United Kingdom Government is in the public domain. This is because it is one of the followin... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Anguilla.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
